.TH KIRO-HWD 8 "2026-11-03" "kiro-hwd" "Kiro system tools"
.SH NAME
kiro-hwd \- pick and install the NVIDIA driver for this machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiro-hwd
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.br
.B kiro-hwd detect
.br
.B kiro-hwd install
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiro-hwd
reads the display devices from sysfs, looks up each NVIDIA device ID in the PCI ID lists mirrored from
CachyOS chwd, and picks one of Kiro's driver profiles:
.TP
.B nvidia-580xx
Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards (the nvidia-580 list).
.TP
.B nouveau
Kepler and older (the nvidia-470, nvidia-390 and nouveau lists): nothing is installed, the open nouveau
driver stays.
.TP
.B nvidia-open
every other NVIDIA card (Turing and newer).
.PP
A laptop (chassis type 8, 9, 10, 11 or 31) with an Intel or AMD iGPU next to the NVIDIA card also gets
nvidia-prime and switcheroo-control for render offload. kiro-hwd does not switch GPU modes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B detect
Show the GPUs, the chosen profile and why. Needs no root.
.TP
.B install
Upgrade the system, then install the profile's packages. Each package comes from the first repo that has it:
the Arch repos, then chaotic-aur, then cachyos. When [cachyos] is commented out in /etc/pacman.conf, a temporary
copy with it enabled is used; /etc/pacman.conf is never changed. 32-bit packages are only added when [multilib]
is enabled. Writes /etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/10-kiro-hwd.conf (early NVIDIA modules) and, on desktops,
10-kiro-hwd-kms.conf (drops the kms hook), and records the result in /var/lib/kiro-hwd/state. Stops when
another NVIDIA driver branch is installed. Run mkinitcpio -P afterwards (the Kiro installer does this).
.TP
.B install \-\-dry\-run
Show the packages and the repo each comes from; install nothing. Needs no root.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KIRO_HWD_SYSFS, KIRO_HWD_CHASSIS
For testing only: read the PCI devices from another directory and use this chassis type.
.SH FILES
.TP
/usr/share/kiro-hwd/profiles.toml
Kiro's driver profiles.
.TP
/usr/share/kiro-hwd/ids/
PCI ID lists from CachyOS chwd (GPL-3.0-or-later); UPSTREAM names the synced commit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR mkinitcpio (8)
